{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564249724,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45d4ea5001O5ckqRhUvI12qP","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","messageID":"msg_1d45d0fc7001Pf1v9q7etmIwSg","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89102a10524c0041","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md","offset":1,"limit":45},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md, lines 1-45\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that write a prompt-free health record on every hook run with a degraded flag and the newest record time, narrow the needs-a-mode label to prompts that name the hub, let the top hub name its routed command, drop the OpenCode compiled-route line, make the brief-cost script read live heads only and fix two behaviour-arm counts and one DSH session id.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"health default and brief refinements tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a build, a daemon restart, a live hook run, a store under the home folder or the full suite. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime` and `HK` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `V <files>` is `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <files>` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed. `VALL` is `V` with no file.\n31: - `MET` is `$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`. `BRF` is `$ADV/lib/skill-advisor-brief.ts`. `FB` is `$HK/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts`. `UPS` is `$HK/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`, `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` and `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`.\n32: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` is `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `REC` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` and `RCT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts`.\n33: - `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy`. `CAP` is `$RA/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, `BASE` is `$RA/command-routing-baseline.json`, `CORPUS` is `$RA/command-prompts.jsonl` and `RAR` is `$RA/README.md`. `SLICE` is `V tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`.\n34: - `S` is `$RA/score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `T` is `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and `VT` is `V tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. `OF` is `$RA/command-offer.mjs` and `VO` is `V tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`. `R` is `$RA/run-command-behaviour.mjs`.\n35: - `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` and `MBCT` is `$ADV/tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts`, a new file.\n36: - `PLG` is `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, authored in place, with `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/opencode/system-skill-advisor.js` a link to it. `NPLT` is `.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` and `NPL` is `node --test $NPLT`, which must report `fail 0`.\n37: - `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts` and `DALL` is `node --test $DS/tests/*.test.cjs`, which must report `fail 0`.\n38: - `HD` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `HV` is `$HK/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md`, `ARCH` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `FC` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`.\n39: - `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`, the shim every hook runtime runs.\n40: - `FINAL` is `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-final.jsonl`, read-only. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n41: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.plain.tune, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached'`.\n42: - `EVAL` is `node $RA/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`.\n43: - `DRV` is `node $ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check`, which must exit 0 and print `\"changed\": []`. `SRM` is `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, which must exit 0.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 46]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md, lines 1-45\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 15: health-default-and-brief-refinements\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that write a prompt-free health record on every hook run with a degraded flag and the newest record time, narrow the needs-a-mode label to prompts that name the hub, let the top hub name its routed command, drop the OpenCode compiled-route line, make the brief-cost script read live heads only and fix