{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564289534,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45df2c2001Hwg7WLpcIbWgL9","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","messageID":"msg_1d45db318001iBi0SJPNTSXxTt","type":"tool","id":"call_5284d33df1634a1da7fb029d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md","limit":60},"output":"Read file .skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Evidence and proof\"\n3: description: \"A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"observed derived inferred\"\n6:   - \"how a green run lies\"\n7:   - \"exit 0 with no output\"\n8:   - \"negative control\"\n9:   - \"watch it fail first\"\n10:   - \"baseline before no regressions\"\n11:   - \"a finding is a hypothesis\"\n12:   - \"the sub-agent said complete\"\n13:   - \"the tool reported success\"\n14:   - \"claiming done\"\n15:   - \"final-state proof\"\n16:   - \"proof plan before implementation\"\n17:   - \"reason from data not memory\"\n18:   - \"the doc disagrees with the code\"\n19:   - \"honest close-out\"\n20:   - \"committed pushed dirty\"\n21:   - \"what only the operator can verify\"\n22:   - \"unconfirmed cause\"\n23:   - \"suspected cause\"\n24:   - \"cause then fix\"\n25:   - \"tests pass\"\n26:   - \"verify before claiming done\"\n27: importance_tier: important\n28: contextType: reference\n29: version: 1.1.1.6\n30: ---\n31: \n32: # Rule: Evidence and proof\n33: \n34: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before making any claim someone will act on.\n35: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n36: \n37: ## Fires when\n38: \n39: - About to say \"done\", \"complete\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", or \"no regressions\".\n40: - About to report a result, a number, a file path, or command output.\n41: - A tool, sub-agent, or reviewer reports success or a finding and you are about to act on it.\n42: - About to write a completion summary, or tick anything off as done.\n43: - You are closing out a turn.\n44: \n45: ## The rule\n46: \n47: **A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it. Every load-bearing claim\n48: carries its receipt, or is explicitly labeled as inferred.**\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 1. THREE TIERS\n53: \n54: | Tier | Meaning | How it must appear |\n55: |------|---------|--------------------|\n56: | **OBSERVED** | You ran it and read the output and exit status | Cite the receipt: the command, the `file:line`, the artifact path |\n57: | **DERIVED** | Follows necessarily from something observed | Show the observation and the step from it |\n58: | **INFERRED** | Plausible, unverified | Say so, and say what would confirm it |\n59: \n60: Prose that mixes the three without marking them reads as if all of it were observed.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md, lines 1-60\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Evidence and proof\"\n3: description: \"A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it, and a receipt confirms only what could have contradicted it. Distinguish observed from derived from inferred.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"observed derived inferred\"\n6:   - \"how a green run lies\"\n7:   - \"exit 0 with no output\"\n8:   - \"negative control\"\n9:   - \"watch it fail first\"\n10:   - \"baseline before no regressions\"\n11:   - \"a finding is a hypothesis\"\n12:   - \"the sub-agent said complete\"\n13:   - \"the tool reported success\"\n14:   - \"claiming done\"\n15:   - \"final-state proof\"\n16:   - \"proof plan before implementation\"\n17:   - \"reason from data not memory\"\n18:   - \"the doc disagrees with the code\"\n19:   - \"honest close-out\"\n20:   - \"committed pushed dirty\"\n21:   - \"what only the operator can verify\"\n22:   - \"unconfirmed cause\"\n23:   - \"suspected cause\"\n24:   - \"cause then fix\"\n25:   - \"tests pass\"\n26:   - \"verify before claiming done\"\n27: importance_tier: important\n28: contextType: reference\n29: version: 1.1.1.6\n30: ---\n31: \n32: # Rule: Evidence and proof\n33: \n34: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before making any claim someone will act on.\n35: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n36: \n37: ## Fires when\n38: \n39: - About to say \"done\", \"complete\", \"works\", \"fixed\", \"passing\", or \"no regressions\".\n40: - About to report a result, a number, a file path, or command output.\n41: - A tool, sub-agent, or reviewer reports success or a finding and you are about to act on it.\n42: - About to write a completion summary, or tick anything off as done.\n43: - You are closing out a turn.\n44: \n45: ## The rule\n46: \n47: **A claim is only as strong as the observation behind it. Every load-bearing claim\n48: carries its receipt, or is explicitly labeled as inferred.**\n49: \n50: ---\n51: \n52: ## 1. THREE TIERS\n53: \n54: | Tier | Meaning | How it must appear |\n55: |------|---------|--------------------|\n56: | **OBSERVED** | You ran it and read the output and exit status | Cite the receipt: the command, the `file:line`, the artifact path |\n57: | **DERIVED** | Follows necessarily from something observed | Show the observation and the step from it |\n58: | **INFERRED** | Plausible, unverified | Say so, and say what would confirm it |\n59: \n60: Prose that mixes the three without marking them reads as if all of it were observed.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 61]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/repo-rules/evidence-and-proof.md\",\"limit\":60}"},"time":{"start":1794564289218,"end":1794564289534}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564289552,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45df01d0016r27lix5wgbzLK","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","messageID":"msg_1d45db318001iBi0SJPNTSXxTt","type":"tool","id":"call_679fdeda7b574106bcced053","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md 2>/dev/null","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"benchmark\nchangelog\ncommand-metadata.json\ndescription.json\nfeature-catalog\ngraph-metadata.json\nhub-router.json\nleaf-aliases.json\nleaf-manifest.json\nleaf-scopes.json\nmanual-testing-playbook\nmode-registry.json\nnode_modules\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nREADME.md\nROUTER.md\nscripts\nshared\nsk-create-agent\nsk-create-benchmark\nsk-create-changelog\nsk-create-command\nsk-create-diff\nsk-create-feature-catalog\nsk-create-frontmatter\nsk-create-goal\nsk-create-manual-testing-playbook\nsk-create-quality-control\nsk-create-readme\nsk-create-repo-rule\nsk-create-skill\nsk-create-with-human-voice\nSKILL.md\n---\ntitle: sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\ndescription: First-class surface router document at the sk-doc hub root (ROUTER.md). hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode should load, emitting canonical (workflowMode, leafResourceId) pairs. Relocated verbatim from shared/references/smart-routing.md (v1.0.0.0) as the ROUTER.md consolidation pattern.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-doc surface router\"\n  - \"doc authoring resource map\"\n  - \"packet leaf resource routing\"\n  - \"surface router pattern\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 2.4.6.0\nrouter_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n\nThe machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis is sk-doc's second-layer (surface) router, first-class at the hub root as\n`ROUTER.md`. The hub selects a workflow mode in [`hub-router.json`](hub-router.json)\n(sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command,\nsk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark,\nsk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter,\nsk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control);\nthis doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local\nleaf resources that mode should load. Every path is either packet-qualified\n(`<packet>/references|assets/…`) or an authored shared-alias disk path (`shared/…`),\nand both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the\ncontract boundary (`sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`).\n`FULL_INVENTORY` is the single explicit full-toolkit intent — no other intent\nenumerates the whole hub.\n\nRouting is two stages: the hub picks the WORKFLOW mode (mode telemetry), this\nrouter picks the LEAVES within it. The two layers stay separate — the hub never\nemits leaf paths, and this router never re-decides the mode.\n\n---\n\n## 2. INTENT MODEL\n\n- **doc-quality leaves** — the validation rules, core standards, evergreen\n  packet-id rule, and the quality-control workflow a request to validate, audit,\n  or score documentation against sk-doc standards loads. Fired by \"documentation\n  quality / validate documentation / validate a document / score this document /\n  DQI / document audit / review the docs / document for clarity / audit the docs /\n  pass review\"\n  requests. The scoring phrases mirror `hub-router.json`, so a request that\n  reaches the quality mode at stage one also reaches its leaves at stage two.\n- **optimization leaves** — the optimization reference and the llms.txt templates\n  a request to compress, trim, or token-optimize a doc, or emit a machine-readable\n  index loads. Fired by \"optimize / token efficiency / llms.txt / reduce tokens /\n  slim down\" requests.\n- **skill-creation leaves** — the skill creation workflow and the skill.md /\n  readme / reference templates a request to scaffold or author a new skill loads.\n  Fired by \"create a skill / skill.md scaffold / resource_map wiring / package a\n  capability\" requests.\n- **parent-hub leaves.** The nested-packet contract, the hub-router schema and\n  the four parent-hub templates a request to build or rewire a parent hub loads.\n  Fired by \"parent hub / parent skill / mode packet / nested workflow packet /\n  mode-registry.json / hub-router.json\" requests, the file names spelled in full\n  so a bare \"hub router\" in an unrelated sentence does not fire it. This is the leaf set for the\n  `sk-create-skill-parent` mode, which shares the `sk-create-skill` packet but\n  not its leaves: a plain skill request must not pull the hub templates.\n- **render-ledger leaves.** The validation reference that explains the render\n  ledger's debt, exempt and pinned records and the doc rewrite guard, and the\n  maintenance workflow that runs the guard before a rewrite is committed. Fired\n  by \"doc rewrite guard / render ledger / render-known-debt.json / exempt from\n  the render checks / kept every claim\" requests. It belongs to the\n  `sk-create-skill` mode, which owns the ledger.\n- **agent-creation leaves.** The agent README and agent template a request to\n  scaffold an OpenCode agent loads. Fired by \"create an agent / new agent /\n  agent frontmatter / permission object / @analyze agent\" requests.\n- **command-creation leaves.** The command README and command template a\n  request to scaffold a slash command loads. Fired by \"create a command / slash\n  command / argument-hint / allowed-tools / thin router\" requests.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"benchmark\nchangelog\ncommand-metadata.json\ndescription.json\nfeature-catalog\ngraph-metadata.json\nhub-router.json\nleaf-aliases.json\nleaf-manifest.json\nleaf-scopes.json\nmanual-testing-playbook\nmode-registry.json\nnode_modules\npackage-lock.json\npackage.json\nREADME.md\nROUTER.md\nscripts\nshared\nsk-create-agent\nsk-create-benchmark\nsk-create-changelog\nsk-create-command\nsk-create-diff\nsk-create-feature-catalog\nsk-create-frontmatter\nsk-create-goal\nsk-create-manual-testing-playbook\nsk-create-quality-control\nsk-create-readme\nsk-create-repo-rule\nsk-create-skill\nsk-create-with-human-voice\nSKILL.md\n---\ntitle: sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\ndescription: First-class surface router document at the sk-doc hub root (ROUTER.md). hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local leaf resources that mode should load, emitting canonical (workflowMode, leafResourceId) pairs. Relocated verbatim from shared/references/smart-routing.md (v1.0.0.0) as the ROUTER.md consolidation pattern.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-doc surface router\"\n  - \"doc authoring resource map\"\n  - \"packet leaf resource routing\"\n  - \"surface router pattern\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 2.4.6.0\nrouter_state: active\nskill_pointer: SKILL.md\n---\n\n# sk-doc Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n\nThe machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). `SKILL.md` keeps the short routing prose and the link that points here; this file holds the declaration a reader parses to decide what loads.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis is sk-doc's second-layer (surface) router, first-class at the hub root as\n`ROUTER.md`. The hub selects a workflow mode in [`hub-router.json`](hub-router.json)\n(sk-create-skill, sk-create-skill-parent, sk-create-readme, sk-create-agent, sk-create-command,\nsk-create-feature-catalog, sk-create-manual-testing-playbook, sk-create-benchmark,\nsk-create-changelog, sk-create-diff, sk-create-repo-rule, sk-create-frontmatter,\nsk-create-goal, sk-create-with-human-voice, or sk-create-quality-control);\nthis doc maps a request's documentation/authoring intent to the exact packet-local\nleaf resources that mode should load. Every path is either packet-qualified\n(`<packet>/references|assets/…`) or an authored shared-alias disk path (`shared/…`),\nand both convert to the canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair at the\ncontract boundary (`sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/lib/leaf-resource-contract.cjs`).\n`FULL_INVENTORY` is the single explicit full-toolkit intent — no other intent\nenumerates the whole hub.\n\nRouting is two stages: the hub picks the WORKFLOW mode (mode telemetry), this\nrouter picks the LEAVES within it. The two layers stay separate — the hub never\nemits leaf paths, and this router never re-decides the mode.\n\n---\n\n## 2. INTENT MODEL\n\n- **doc-quality leaves** — the validation rules, core standards, evergreen\n  packet-id rule, and the quality-control workflow a request to validate, audit,\n  or score documentation against sk-doc standards loads. Fired by \"documentation\n  quality / validate documentation / validate a document / score this document /\n  DQI / document audit / review the docs / document for clarity / audit the docs /\n  pass review\"\n  requests. The scoring phrases mirror `hub-router.json`, so a request that\n  reaches the quality mode at stage one also reaches its leaves at stage two.\n- **optimization leaves** — the optimization reference and the llms.txt templates\n  a request to compress, trim, or token-optimize a doc, or emit a machine-readable\n  index loads. Fired by \"optimize / token efficiency / llms.txt / reduce tokens /\n  slim down\" requests.\n- **skill-creation leaves** — the skill creation workflow and the skill.md /\n  readme / reference templates a request to scaffold or author a new skill loads.\n  Fired by \"create a skill / skill.md scaffold / resource_map wiring / package a\n  capability\" requests.\n- **parent-hub leaves.** The nested-packet contract, the hub-router schema and\n  the four parent-hub templates a request to build or rewire a parent hub loads.\n  Fired by \"parent hub / parent skill / mode packet / nested workflow packet /\n  mode-registry.json / hub-router.json\" requests, the file names spelled in full\n  so a bare \"hub router\" in an unrelated sentence does not fire it. This is the leaf set for the\n  `sk-create-skill-parent` mode, which shares the `sk-create-skill` packet but\n  not its leaves: a plain skill request must not pull the hub templates.\n- **render-ledger leaves.** The validation reference that explains the render\n  ledger's debt, exempt and pinned records and the doc rewrite guard, and the\n  maintenance workflow that runs the guard before a rewrite is committed. Fired\n  by \"doc rewrite guard / render ledger / render-known-debt.json / exempt from\n  the render checks / kept every claim\" requests. It belongs to the\n  `sk-create-skill` mode, which owns the ledger.\n- **agent-creation leaves.** The agent README and agent template a request to\n  scaffold an OpenCode agent loads. Fired by \"create an agent / new agent /\n  agent frontmatter / permission object / @analyze agent\" requests.\n- **command-creation leaves.** The command README and command template a\n  request to scaffold a slash command loads. Fired by \"create a command / slash\n  command / argument-hint / allowed-tools / thin router\" requests.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"ls .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,80p' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md 2>/dev/null\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794564288541,"end":1794564289552}}}}
