{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564322416,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","part":{"partID":"prt_1d45e71de001E9uO0EzlJ4R57R","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","messageID":"msg_1d45e5be7001rATxKUxNyIFIFn","type":"tool","id":"call_3df5f067dc1844fc97acbe59","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\nindex 41ac325ddc..a7431a2558 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\n@@ -150 +150 @@ Validation runs at two layers.\n-**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). The code writes them only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n+**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\nindex 41ac325ddc..a7431a2558 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\n@@ -150 +150 @@ Validation runs at two layers.\n-**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). The code writes them only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n+**Release validation.** `advisor_validate` runs the regression suite and reports threshold semantics (aggregate vs runtime) plus a prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals` block. Hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks so `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes. Records carry the runtime that served the turn, the bytes delivered (`emittedBytes`) and whether the directives were suppressed (`directivesSuppressed`). Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` adds the skill label and the error text. The bounded trim writes a temp file and renames it over the log so a crash mid-trim keeps the old log.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794564321759,"end":1794564322416}}}}
