{"type":"text","timestamp":1794564334698,"sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","part":{"id":"prt_1d45e9f4c0013uO6jeRu6fOugB","sessionID":"ses_e2ba44aa3ffeaCSqLtdsNQ8wes","messageID":"msg_1d45e8b3d001XTTdTs7Fp89dqj","type":"text","text":"T010 done.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md` — one sentence replaced in the **Release validation** paragraph of section 6 (line 150). Old: `The code writes them only when \\`SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\` is set.` New: `Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and \\`SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG\\` adds the skill label and the error text.`\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"writes them only when\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\n(no output)\nexit=1\n\n$ rg -c \"adds the skill label and the error text\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nBoth halves match the task's expectation: first prints nothing, second prints `1`.\n\n**Scope check** — `git diff --stat` for the file: `1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)`. No other file touched, no git state changed, checkbox in `tasks.md` left unticked.\n\n**Could not do** — nothing. No verification step was skipped; the task's Verify is `rg`-only, so no typecheck or vitest run applied.\n\nOne thing worth flagging, not acted on: the new sentence names \"skill label\" twice (\"with no prompt, skill label or error text, and … adds the skill label and the error text\"), which reads slightly repetitive. That is the task's verbatim wording, so I kept it exactly as specified rather than smoothing it.","time":{"start":1794564333388,"end":1794564334698}}}
